{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Let it redeem it</b> — From לחם מגואל. And some say: it is from גאל, and its meaning is that they would redeem it and draw it to themselves, though it is far." "<b>Let it terrify it</b> — Let it frighten it, so that it not stand, like יבעתתו רוח רעה." "<b>Like the bitter things of day</b> — Like קטב מרירי. And some say: the kaf is like כחצי הלילה, like כמסיגי גבול." "And the meaning of מרירי יום — the intensity of the heat that resembles a death-poison, and if he was born at night, that night, darkness will take him."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:36.526002215Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}